=== ① stage 2: agent-as-release-gate live E2E (2026-07-26, kind, $0) ===

WHAT THIS PROVES
  The platform-agent's own detect->analyze->decide pipeline runs as an Argo
  Rollouts AnalysisTemplate (`web` provider). The in-cluster analyzer has no
  model, so every judgement is `unknown` -- and `successCondition: result ==
  "pass"` does not hold for `unknown`. The rollout therefore aborts WITH NO
  HUMAN ACTION. "Cannot judge" != "approved".

  This is the asymmetry the gate is built around: wrongly aborting a good
  release costs a retry, wrongly promoting a bad one ships it.

TERRAFORM WIRING (new this run)
  Stage 2 shipped with chart values but no module variables, which left
  `helm upgrade --set` as the only way to enable it -- and that drifts the
  release out from under the Terraform state that owns it. Now:
    terraform apply -var rollouts_demo_agent_analysis_enabled=true
  plan = 0 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy (only helm_release.rollouts_demo).

  Independently switchable, verified live: with stage 1 (`analysis.enabled`)
  left false, only ONE template is installed --
    $ kubectl get analysistemplate -n argo-rollouts
    NAME                          AGE
    rollouts-demo-agent-verdict   69s
  and the Rollout lists only that judge under canary.analysis.templates.

--- before ---
phase=Healthy image=argoproj/rollouts-demo:red
judges wired: rollouts-demo-agent-verdict   (stage 1 metric judge OFF)

--- the gate endpoint, called from INSIDE the cluster ---
HTTP 200 {"verdict": "unknown", "confidence": 0.0,
          "reason": "analysis confidence 0.00 below 0.40 -- refusing to promote
                     on an untrustworthy judgment",
          "severity": "P2", "runbook_id": "generic-recovery",
          "details": {"actions": ["ONPREM-CreateChangeRequest"],
                      "remediation_mode": "APPROVE", "trace_id": ""}}

  200 with a verdict body => the gate is REACHABLE. Everything below is a
  JUDGEMENT failure, not a connectivity failure. (That distinction is the whole
  point: an unreachable judge and an unsure judge must both block, but they are
  different defects and the evidence has to tell them apart.)

--- trigger a canary (red -> blue) ---
rollout.argoproj.io/rollouts-demo patched

--- watch (abort expected ~90s: initialDelay 30s + interval 60s, failureLimit 1) ---
