--- NOT SHOWN: the pass path ---
  Every verdict in this cluster is `unknown` because the in-cluster analyzer has
  no model, so this run cannot demonstrate that a HEALTHY release is promoted.
  Read honestly: this proves the gate BLOCKS, not that it discriminates. The
  unit suite covers the pass branch (tests/test_canary_judge.py), but a live
  pass needs a model the cluster can reach.

  Reachability re-measured this run, from inside the pa webhook pod:
    host.docker.internal -> 192.168.65.254   HTTP 200
    192.168.65.254       -> 192.168.65.254   HTTP 200
    host.lima.internal   -> DNS-FAIL
  So the earlier note that the host is "behind the Docker VM gateway and
  unreachable" is WRONG -- pods do reach the host. The actual blockers are:
    (1) MLX is not running (`make local-llm-status` -> MLX-LM :18090 down), and
    (2) MLX and the tool-call proxy bind to 127.0.0.1, so reaching them from the
        cluster needs a bind change (0.0.0.0 = LAN exposure, a user decision).
  With those resolved, ANALYZER_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:18091/v1
  on the webhook deployment should light up the pass path.

--- restored ---
  Gate returned to its default-OFF state (terraform apply with no -var) and the
  rollout returned to the stable image, so the documented Phase 4 manual
  promote/abort demo is unchanged.

